  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to have applications with statuses that lack corresponding audit entries. The AuditCompleteness assertion directly checks that every status has exactly one audit entry; without the fact, Alloy will construct a counterexample where an application has a status but no audit entry.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfApproval  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfApproval.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows officers to approve applications where they are the applicant. The FR_013 and NoSelfMutation assertions verify that this never happens; without the fact, Alloy will find a counterexample with an officer deciding their own application.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_NoSelfApprovalOrDecision, NoSelfMutation
      - FR_013_NoSelfApprovalOrDecision: PASS (vacuous?)
      - NoSelfMutation: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AssignedOfficerOnly  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AssignedOfficerOnly.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows any officer to patch any application, even if they are not assigned. The FR_012 assertion verifies that status changes only come from the assigned officer; without the fact, Alloy will construct a counterexample with an unassigned officer changing status.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch
      - FR_012_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ValidTransitions  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_ValidTransitions.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows invalid status transitions such as pending → approved (skipping under_review). The FR_009 assertion verifies that only the documented transitions occur; without the fact, Alloy will find a counterexample with an invalid transition.
    expected to FAIL: FR_009_ValidStatusMachine
      - FR_009_ValidStatusMachine: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the permission matrix to be undefined or incorrect. The LeastPrivilege, FR_003, and FR_005 assertions verify the correctness of role-operation permissions; without the fact, Alloy will construct a model where forbidden operations appear to be allowed.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_003_ApplicantPermissions, FR_005_AuditorCannotWrite
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_ApplicantPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_AuditorCannotWrite: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerApplicant  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerApplicant.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows applicants to have multiple in-flight applications simultaneously. The FR_008 assertion verifies the one-in-flight constraint; without the fact, Alloy will find a counterexample with duplicate pending/under_review applications for the same applicant.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant: FAIL (expected)

